  for scale: the median human inter-turn gap is ~200 ms (Stivers et al. 2009),
  so this is on the order of one whole conversational beat per exchange.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE ON ABSOLUTE LEVELS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Absolute FIR is high across ALL systems because every VAD pause > 150 ms
  in 4-party AMI meeting speech counts as a decision point, and the median
  hold lasts 576 ms. Meeting speech pauses far more than a 2-party support
  call. The comparison is controlled — identical decision points, identical
  delays, identical policy family — so the RELATIVE gap transfers even though
  the absolute level is domain-specific.

fusion reduces mean false-interruption rate over the 0.15-1.5 s band
by 17.7% relative to the fixed-threshold baseline.

